  "pli-tv-bu-vb-ss1:2.2.11": "“Gives the trial period” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>mānattaṁ deti</i>. For the meaning of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>mānatta</i> see Bhikkhu Ñāṇatusita, “Analysis of the Bhikkhu Pātimokkha”, p. 123. | The point here, which can only be understood from the Pali, is that the word <i lang='pi' translate='no'>saṅghādisesa</i> (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>saṅgha</i> + <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ādisesa</i>) is derived from the fact that only the <i lang='pi' translate='no'>saṅgha</i> can do the legal procedures required when a monastic commits this offense. | “Several” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sambahula</i>. See Appendix of Technical Terms for a discussion of this rendering. ",
